<title>UK: BOE gives UK money market 404 mln stg further help.</title>
<headline>BOE gives UK money market 404 mln stg further help.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-01-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Bank of England said it provided the UK money market with a further 404 million stg of assistance at established interest rates.  </p>
<p>			    EARLY	1200 GMT   1400 GMT   LATE</p>
<p> FORECAST SHORTAGE    1.15 BLN   1.15 BLN   1.2 BLN    =</p>
<p> CUMULATIVE SUPPLY    =	    314 MLN    718 MLN    =</p>
<p> DETAILS</p>
<p> BAND 1  BANK BILLS   =	     26 MLN*    52 MLN*   =</p>
<p> BAND 2  BANK BILLS   =	     58 MLN*   302 MLN*   =</p>
<p> BILLS/FRG TO FEB 17  =	    230 MLN!    50 MLN!</p>
<p>* INTEREST RATE - 5-15/16 PCT (INDICATES UNCHANGED BASE RATES)</p>
<p>! INTEREST RATE 5-31/32 PCT (INDICATES UNCHANGED BASE RATES)</p>
</text>
